## 9. Reviewing someone else's text

Use the same rules, plus these notes from the graded rounds.

- **Lean toward slop on close calls.** About three in four past misses came from calling a line fine when the gold answer said slop. The exceptions are the forms in Section 7.
- **Be strict with** titles, subtitles, kickers, body sentences, action bullets, callouts, closing lines, quotes, footers and source notes.
- **Be lenient with** plain names from the prompt, generic section and column headers, number-plus-noun metric tiles, factual lines built on specific figures, related "&" pairs, short accurate lead-ins, and claims that an on-slide badge or number supports.
- **Check the prompt for every label.** A label the prompt never mentions usually fails ("Where did this come from?"). Prompt wording can still fail when it is awkward or unclear ("drop-in", "whole-life performance").
- **Judge wording only.** Symbol placement (+3,000), common abbreviations ("Design and tech."), repeated KPI figures and doubts about chart grouping do not make a line slop.
- **Keep parallel items consistent.** Three matching subtitles or three matching quotes usually share one verdict.
- **Write each justification as one plain sentence** that quotes the exact words, names the problem and, where useful, gives the plain fix. Use plain ASCII with straight quotes.

| Label type | Example | Verdict |
|---|---|---|
| Project or topic name from the brief | PROJECT RENA, VIETNAM ECONOMIC OUTLOOK | Not slop |
| Kicker that restates the title | PEAK SEASON 2025 | Slop |
| Department or generic kicker nobody asked for | BIOPHARMA ANALYTICAL DEVELOPMENT | Slop |
| Section header that restates the title in new words | Federal Records Warranting Follow-Up | Slop |
| Generic header that matches its content | Purpose, KEY TAKEAWAYS | Not slop |
| Label whose adjective does not fit the content | Regulatory intent | Slop |
| Meta footer | Internal planning discussion | Slop |
| Number plus plain noun | 50+ Active customers | Not slop |
| Number plus jargon | c.150 Consulting FTEs | Slop |
| Related "&" pair | Affordability & flexibility | Not slop |
| Unrelated "&" pair | Revenue & public trust | Slop |
| Synonym pair | PPP RISK / COST | Slop |
